## New Capabilities Identified

- **Swim-lane layout mode**: a second, additive graph rendering mode inspired directly by Nate Herk's "AI Stack, Connected" demo — up to 4 horizontal lanes grouped by existing folder/taxonomy field, pill-shaped labeled nodes, edges hidden until a node is clicked, then animated curved connector lines draw from the clicked node to its related nodes. No camera pan/zoom in this mode (static board).
- **Layout mode toggle**: a persistent UI control switching between force-directed (existing, unchanged) and swim-lane (new) rendering, with no data refetch — both modes render from the same `graph-data.json`.
- **Lane-capping rule**: folders beyond the 4 largest/most-populated collapse into a single "Other" lane, to guarantee the board fits without a scrollbar.

## Priority Signal

- The user was explicit that the original inspiration reference (Nate Herk's tiered/pill/animated-connection demo) was the actual intended visual, and that the currently-built force-directed graph (epic baPTSK2, already Complete) reads as "too messy" on its own.
- However, the user wants the toggle to **add** swim-lane mode alongside force-directed, not replace it — de-risking the change relative to already-completed and already-verified TOR-02 requirements for force-directed mode.
- Swim-lane mode's defining interaction (animated on-click connector-line draw, static board) is the priority; force-directed mode requires no behavior change at all.

## Deferred Items

- The exact bucketing rule for which folders get their own lane vs. collapse into "Other" (e.g., top-N by node count vs. a manually curated list) is deferred to requirements capture / epic planning — flagged as an open risk in ConOps §8, not resolved in this discovery pass.
- Whether `react-force-graph`'s fixed-position (`fx`/`fy`) mode can support the swim-lane visual and animation requirements, or whether a separate custom renderer is needed, is deferred to a technical spike (same open-risk entry).
- No changes were made to the public vault's actual taxonomy/folder content (still seed/placeholder — only `concepts/` and `sources/` exist) — real lane assignment can't be finalized until the 40+-reference research vault is ingested (Product Vision §6, unchanged item).
